{"units": [{"id": "apollymi-quote9", "translation": "You destroyed the city by honoring newcomers."}, {"id": "apollymi-quote10", "translation": "O Zeus, pity our toils and us who are perishing (thus I wrote for μὴ ἀπολωλότας [not perishing])."}, {"id": "apollymi-quote11", "translation": "And the whole army was perishing."}, {"id": "apollymi-quote12", "translation": "He perished gloriously."}, {"id": "apollymi-quote13", "translation": "Just as his father perished."}, {"id": "apollymi-word1", "translation": "he destroyed this"}, {"id": "apollymi-word2", "translation": "he destroyed"}, {"id": "apollymi-word3", "translation": "the things that have perished"}, {"id": "apollymi-word4", "translation": "my things that have perished"}, {"id": "apollymi-word5", "translation": "I have perished"}, {"id": "apollymi-word6", "translation": "I am perishing"}, {"id": "apollon-orth1", "translation": "Apollo"}, {"id": "apollon-def1", "translation": "Apollo."}, {"id": "apollon-note1", "translation": "In M ὤπολλον ὤπολλον [O Apollo, O Apollo] (and the crasis πολλον [Apollo] is mentioned in Etym. M. p. 514, 30), but at 1080 and 1085 ἄπολλον ἀπολλον | ἀγυιᾶτ᾽, ἀπόλλων ἐμός [O Apollo, O Apollo, god of streets, my destroyer] (i.e., ἀπολλὺς ἐμέ [destroying me], deriving the name Ἀπόλλων [Apollo] from ἀπόλλυμι [I destroy]). I restored Απολλον Απολλον [Apollo, Apollo] in the first two places as well. For the meter demands either this or bacchei, with Απόλλων [Apollo] repeated four times, as Hermann did."}, {"id": "apollon-note2", "translation": "Vocative"}, {"id": "apollon-quote1", "translation": "O dear Apollo."}, {"id": "apollon-quote2", "translation": "The might of Apollo."}, {"id": "apollon-quote3", "translation": "The august lord Apollo of the seventh day."}, {"id": "apollon-quote4", "translation": "And the highest one hearing, whether Apollo or Pan or Zeus."}, {"id": "apollon-quote5", "translation": "Apollo the prophet set me upon this office."}, {"id": "apollon-quote6", "translation": "Lycean Apollo."}, {"id": "apollon-quote7", "translation": "Apollo himself stripping me of my prophetic robe."}, {"id": "apollon-quote8", "translation": "Lord Apollo."}, {"id": "apollon-quote9", "translation": "Lord Apollo,"}, {"id": "apollon-quote10", "translation": "Neither Apollo nor Athena's might could save you."}, {"id": "apollon-quote11", "translation": "Guide me, Apollo."}, {"id": "apollon-quote12", "translation": "O Phoebus Apollo."}, {"id": "apollon-quote13", "translation": "And holy Apollo, an exile from heaven, a god."}, {"id": "apollon-quote14", "translation": "The healer-prophet, son of Apollo."}, {"id": "apollon-quote15", "translation": "And may Apollo the hunter guide the arrow straight."}, {"id": "apollon-quote16", "translation": "Apollo of the ivy."}, {"id": "apollon-quote17", "translation": "The untrodden one to Apollo."}, {"id": "apollon-word1", "translation": "O Apollo, O Apollo"}, {"id": "apollon-word2", "translation": "Apollo"}, {"id": "apollon-word3", "translation": "O Apollo, O Apollo, god of streets, my destroyer"}, {"id": "apollon-word4", "translation": "destroying me"}, {"id": "apollon-word5", "translation": "Apollo"}, {"id": "apollon-word6", "translation": "I destroy"}, {"id": "apollon-word7", "translation": "Apollo, Apollo"}, {"id": "apollon-word8", "translation": "Apollo"}, {"id": "apomousos-orth1", "translation": "estranged from the Muses, i.e. unmusical"}, {"id": "apomousos-def1", "translation": "estranged from the Muses, i.e. unmusical"}, {"id": "apomousos-note1", "translation": "Adverb"}, {"id": "apomousos-note2", "translation": "where Elmsley [reads] ἀπόμουσός τ' οὔτ᾽ [unmusical and neither]"}, {"id": "apomousos-quote1", "translation": "You were written very unmusically, and not steering the helm of your mind well."}, {"id": "apomousos-word1", "translation": "unmusical"}, {"id": "apomousos-word2", "translation": "Adverb"}, {"id": "apomousos-word3", "translation": "unmusical and neither"}, {"id": "aponos-orth1", "translation": "free from toil"}, {"id": "aponos-def1", "translation": "free from toil"}, {"id": "aponos-note1", "translation": "Hermann for - ποινον [blood-price]"}, {"id": "aponos-quote1", "translation": "And returns from wars free from toil, unharmed, they led to their homes."}, {"id": "aponos-quote2", "translation": "force without toil"}, {"id": "aponos-word1", "translation": "blood-price"}, {"id": "apoxenos-orth1", "translation": "not received as a guest"}, {"id": "apoxenos-def1", "translation": "not received as a guest"}, {"id": "apoxenos-def2", "translation": "exile"}, {"id": "apoxenos-quote1", "translation": "A stranger to this land."}, {"id": "apoxenos-quote2", "translation": "A wandering exile, a stranger to this land."}, {"id": "apoxenos-quote3", "translation": "And I am a wanderer, a stranger to this land."}, {"id": "apopempomai-orth1", "translation": "to send away (middle form)"}, {"id": "apopempomai-def1", "translation": "(middle form) I send away"}, {"id": "apopempomai-quote1", "translation": "Having sent away the spear-wielding, impetuous bedmate."}, {"id": "apopolis-orth1", "translation": "exiled from the city"}, {"id": "apopolis-def1", "translation": "exiled from the city"}, {"id": "apopolis-note1", "translation": "Thus Seidler for άπολις [cityless]"}, {"id": "apopolis-quote1", "translation": "And you will be exiled from the city."}, {"id": "apopolis-word1", "translation": "cityless"}, {"id": "apoptystos-orth1", "translation": "abominable, hated"}, {"id": "apoptystos-def1", "translation": "abominable, hated"}, {"id": "apoptystos-quote1", "translation": "Abominable to the gods."}, {"id": "apoptyo-orth1", "translation": "to spit out"}, {"id": "apoptyo-def1", "translation": "I spit out"}, {"id": "apoptyo-def2", "translation": "I abhor, I reject"}, {"id": "apoptyo-quote1", "translation": "One must spit out and purify the mouth."}, {"id": "apoptyo-quote2", "translation": "Do you not answer, but spit out my words?"}, {"id": "apoptyo-quote3", "translation": "And there is no disease which I would rather spit out than this."}, {"id": "apoptyo-quote4", "translation": "Nor does he sit having spat out the judgment of hard-to-interpret dreams, with persuasive confidence."}, {"id": "apoptyo-quote5", "translation": "And in turn they spat upon the marriage bed of their brother."}, {"id": "apoptyo-quote6", "translation": "To spit out this lock of hair."}, {"id": "aporthetos-orth1", "translation": "not destroyed, safe"}, {"id": "aporthetos-def1", "translation": "not destroyed, safe"}, {"id": "aporthetos-quote1", "translation": "Is the city of Athens still not destroyed?"}, {"id": "aporos-orth1", "translation": "difficult to do"}, {"id": "aporos-def1", "translation": "difficult to do"}, {"id": "aporos-quote1", "translation": "This war is without war (I wrote ἀπολέμιστος [unwarlike]), providing resources for the resourceless."}, {"id": "aporreo-orth1", "translation": "to flow away"}, {"id": "aporreo-def1", "translation": "I flow away"}, {"id": "aporreo-note1", "translation": "Passive form of the aorist"}, {"id": "aporreo-quote1", "translation": "Of the blood of those who died well flowing away."}, {"id": "aporregnymi-orth1", "translation": "to break off"}, {"id": "aporregnymi-def1", "translation": "I break off"}, {"id": "aporregnymi-quote1", "translation": "But it is good for him who most quickly broke off the breath of life."}, {"id": "aporripto-orth1", "translation": "to throw away"}, {"id": "aporripto-def1", "translation": "I throw away"}, {"id": "aporripto-quote1", "translation": "I did not throw you into a house of spear-friends."}, {"id": "aporripto-quote2", "translation": "And Cypris has been dishonorably cast aside by this argument."}, {"id": "aporripto-quote3", "translation": "Let not my word be cast aside."}, {"id": "apophanizo-orth1", "translation": "to bereave"}, {"id": "apophanizo-def1", "translation": "I bereave"}, {"id": "apophanizo-note1", "translation": "Passive"}]}